{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review as requested. The review included a complete trace of all claims, numbered parts, figure descriptions, and other technical assertions in the draft against the authoritative inventor source files. While most of the draft is well-supported and internally consistent, I found one critical disclosure-fidelity issue concerning the location of a functional component and one minor issue of internal consistency in the figure briefs.\n\nThe critical issue is that the draft's depiction of the temperature-responsive latch places it outside the insulated shell, a specific and functionally significant location that is not supported by the inventor's disclosure. The inventor's description implies the latch is thermally coupled to the internal phase-change cassette, and therefore should be located inside the shell. This unsupported choice must be corrected.\n\nThe minor issue involves figure briefs that refer to numbered parts as \"unnumbered,\" which should be corrected for clarity and consistency. The findings below provide the exact locations, evidence, and corrective text for each issue. After these corrections are made, the application should be ready for the next stage of review."}
